  "preview": "Three-act task. A phone shows 41 GB used out of 64 GB. Each minute of video takes about the same chunk. How long until storage runs out?",
  "body": {
    "goal": "Estimate, model, and solve a two-step inequality from a multimedia scenario, with an explicit estimation phase before computation, and interpret the answer in concrete time units.",
    "studentPrompt": "**ACT 1 — The Hook**\n\nIsaiah is at a school dance. His phone shows:\n\n- Total storage: 64 GB\n- Used: 41 GB\n- He's recording video continuously for the rest of the night.\n\nHe estimates each minute of HD video uses about 0.18 GB of storage. The phone will stop recording when storage hits the full 64 GB.\n\n1. WITHOUT calculating — just estimate. Will the phone last 30 more minutes? An hour? Three hours? Write down your gut guess with a number and a reason.\n\n**ACT 2 — The Math**\n\n2. Let m be the number of additional minutes of video Isaiah records. Write an inequality that represents the phone STILL having storage available (used <= 64 GB).\n3. Solve the inequality. How long can Isaiah keep recording?\n4. Convert your answer to hours, minutes, and seconds.\n\n**ACT 3 — The Reveal**\n\n5. The dance has 1 hour and 45 minutes left. Will Isaiah's phone make it to the end of the dance? By how much?\n6. Isaiah could clear out 8 GB of old photos before he starts. Rewrite the inequality. How much MORE recording time does that buy him?\n7. He could also switch to standard definition video, which uses 0.06 GB per minute. Without re-solving, just predict: roughly how many times longer will the phone record? Then check by solving.",
    "image": {
      "alt": "A smartphone in portrait orientation showing a storage bar that is mostly filled with a label '41 of 64 GB used' and a small camera icon at the top.",
      "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 220\" font-family=\"system-ui, sans-serif\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"480\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#f0eee9\"/><g transform=\"translate(180,15)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"120\" height=\"195\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#1f2a44\"/><rect x=\"6\" y=\"10\" width=\"108\" height=\"175\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8f0f7\"/><rect x=\"45\" y=\"2\" width=\"30\" height=\"6\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#1f2a44\"/><g transform=\"translate(20,25)\"><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#b03a3a\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"2\" width=\"10\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#b03a3a\"/></g><text x=\"60\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1f2a44\">Storage</text><rect x=\"15\" y=\"60\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#d8e0e8\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"60\" width=\"57.7\" height=\"14\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#d94f4f\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1f2a44\">41 of 64 GB</text><g transform=\"translate(30,110)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"6\" width=\"50\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1f2a44\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"0\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#1f2a44\"/><circle cx=\"25\" cy=\"22\" r=\"10\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f6e9c8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"25\" cy=\"22\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f6e9c8\"/><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"12\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#d94f4f\"/></g><text x=\"60\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6b7280\">Recording...</text><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"178\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#d94f4f\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0.2;1\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></circle></g><g fill=\"#1f2a44\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\"><text x=\"30\" y=\"110\">0.18 GB</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"125\">per minute</text></g><g fill=\"#1f2a44\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\"><text x=\"380\" y=\"110\">Dance ends:</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"125\">1h 45m</text></g></svg>"
    },
    "launch": "ACT 1 only. Show the image. Read the situation. Ask the estimation question and require a number from every group BEFORE they touch math. Write the range of guesses on the board. Then release them to Act 2.",
    "materials": [
      "Vertical whiteboards",
      "Markers",
      "Calculator allowed",
      "Timer or clock for Act 1 estimation"
    ],
    "concepts": [
      "two-step-inequalities",
      "real-world-modeling",
      "estimation",
